{% set local_problem %}
<p>Hazel Green's appeal is space and quiet — larger lots, mature trees, a residential feel. But those trees are constantly shedding debris into your gutters, and every seam in a traditional gutter system is a place for that debris to catch and a point where leaks develop.</p>

<p>Many Hazel Green homes, especially newer construction, came with builder-grade sectional gutters — the cheapest option that technically meets code. These gutters have seams every 10 feet, thin-gauge materials that dent easily, and are often undersized for North Alabama's heavy rainfall. After a few years, they start leaking, sagging, and overflowing.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve these problems at the source. No seams means no leaks. Custom fabrication means gutters that fit your specific roofline. Heavy-gauge aluminum means durability that lasts decades, not years.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Hazel Green home, measure your roofline, and fabricate gutters right in your driveway. The result is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your home — not generic sections forced to fit.</p>
{% endset %}

